  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [Fire safety strategy, Plant Noise Impact Assessment, Standard-soundproofing received 24/10/2025\r\n8644 / PL-01 Rev A, G1 received 03/11/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to use, all details of the emergency generator shall be submitted to and approved by the local authority to confirm that sound emitted by standby or emergency generators during power outages or testing does not exceed the lowest daytime ambient noise level LAeq(15min) as measured or calculated according to BS4142:2014. \r\nFor the purpose of testing, testing is permitted for up to 1 hour per month between 09.00 and 17.00 Monday to Friday only and not on public holidays.\r\nReason: To ensure that the proposed development does not prejudice the amenities of occupiers of neighbouring properties\r\nNOTE: The applicant should also submit historical records of power outages in the area incl. times and duration of power outages where available, and the proposed times/ frequency and duration of testing. "
